Ported from laya/calibrate.py at commit 432312b36714: _select_abstention_threshold (one pseudo-error added
so a short clean run does not clear the gate, ties judged as a whole) and the rule that a cut is fitted on
the scale the gate compares.

Changes made in calibaudit: rewritten for binary forecasts in the Python standard library (no numpy);
clusters are days; equal-mass reliability bins by default; an optional probit link; a forward split
(fit on the first two thirds of the days, judge on the rest); the bootstrap runs on per-day sums; a
rule-of-three bound replaces the interval when no errors are observed.
